  message: "PR-1 of 3 LANDED (PR #408, dev 158d4d3ab1): the Python C3 MRO walker (_walk_c3) registered in _MRO_WALKERS activates Site-2 Step-2 for Python — typed receivers (WI-noham Part A receiver_type_hint) calling an INHERITED method now resolve to the ancestor's method via true C3 linearization (ast_call_inherited_method @0.70, calls->method; python kept OUT of _LEGACY_SITE2_LANGS so strict Site-2 holds). C3 (not insertion-order BFS) verified vs 44k+ CPython __mro__; adversarial review (wf_631a95db-7a2) caught + fixed a base-order blocker (reorder Python bases from meta['base_classes'] — qualified in-tree bases arrive out of order) and a depth/cycle wrong-positive (bias to unresolved). Behavioral evidence: +120 inherited-method calls resolved on hypergumbo self-analysis. Filed INV-guviv (external-base blind spot, shared w/ all walkers). STAYS OPEN — remaining WI-hiziz pieces: PR-2 = Site-1 self.method() enclosing_class emission (py.py), PR-3 = Site-3 self.field.method() inherited_field_receiver + meta['fields'] (py.py). Both rebase on this walker."  # b37f
